# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# ARIA Framework — Environment Configuration Template
# Copy to .env and fill in real values. NEVER commit .env to git.
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# ── Application Under Test ─────────────────────────────────────────────
AUT_BASE_URL=https://www.saucedemo.com/
AUT_ENVIRONMENT=staging

# ── Playwright ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PLAYWRIGHT_HEADLESS=true
PLAYWRIGHT_WORKERS=4
# PLAYWRIGHT_TIMEOUT=30000           # Per-test budget. Left unset it is derived from the budgets below,
                                     # so an explicit value here can silently undercut them.
PLAYWRIGHT_RETRIES=2
# PLAYWRIGHT_EXPECT_TIMEOUT=10000    # Budget for one web-first assertion (expect(locator).toBeVisible()
                                     # and friends). Playwright's own default is 5s regardless of the
                                     # action budget; an assertion that waits on a server round trip —
                                     # the dashboard after a sign-in submit — needs more than one click
                                     # does. Defaults to PLAYWRIGHT_ACTION_TIMEOUT.

# ── Jira MCP Integration ───────────────────────────────────────────────
JIRA_BASE_URL=https://yourcompany.atlassian.net
JIRA_EMAIL=your-email@company.com
JIRA_API_TOKEN=your-jira-api-token
JIRA_PROJECT_KEY=SD
JIRA_BOARD_ID=35

# ── Gmail SMTP ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GMAIL_USER=your-qa-bot@gmail.com
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=your-app-password
GMAIL_FROM=ARIA QA Bot <your-qa-bot@gmail.com>
GMAIL_TO=qa-lead@yopmail.com,dev-team@yopmail.com

# ── Framework ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
FRAMEWORK_LOG_LEVEL=info
FRAMEWORK_PROJECT_ID=my-project
# manual = human approval required between stages
# auto   = CI mode, skips approval gates (TEST FRAMEWORK USE ONLY)
FRAMEWORK_APPROVAL_MODE=manual
FRAMEWORK_MAX_THREADS=4
SELF_REVIEW_RETRIES=2
SPEC_BATCH_SIZE=10
# Agent 02: max scenarios per test type per user story (min is always 1 per selected type)
# AGENT02_MAX_TC_PER_TYPE=4

# ── K6 Performance Testing ─────────────────────────────────────────────
K6_VUS=10
K6_DURATION=30s
K6_THRESHOLD_P95=500

# ── AWS Bedrock (primary LLM, API key) ─────────────────────────────────
# Bedrock API key sent as a bearer token; Gemini below is the fallback when Bedrock throttles.
AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=your-bedrock-api-key
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# Bedrock model or inference-profile IDs enabled in your account/region.
# Each agent uses its own variable, else BEDROCK_MODEL_DEFAULT (also used by Agents 08/09 and utilities).
BEDROCK_MODEL_DEFAULT=
LLM_MODEL_01=
LLM_MODEL_02=
LLM_MODEL_05=
LLM_MODEL_06=
LLM_MODEL_10=
# Optional output token ceiling for Bedrock (default 8192)
# BEDROCK_MAX_TOKENS=8192
# Cache the system prompt on Bedrock (Claude/Nova) and Anthropic — set false to disable (default true)
# LLM_PROMPT_CACHE=true

# ── LLM Models ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
# Default model for general tasks (e.g. Analysis, Review)
LLM_MODEL_DEFAULT=gemini-3.5-flash
# Specialized model for code generation (e.g. Playwright scripts)
LLM_MODEL_CODING=gemini-3.5-flash
# Specialized model for data generation (e.g. Test data)
LLM_MODEL_DATA=gemini-3.5-flash
# Model for generating vector embeddings
OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# How long (ms) a working fallback model stays pinned per stage across runs before the primary is retried
LLM_FALLBACK_PIN_TTL_MS=1800000

# ── Cost Display (INR) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Live USD→INR rate is fetched from FX_RATE_API_URL and cached in .state/fx-rate-cache.json
# (refreshed every 6h). Set USD_TO_INR_RATE to pin a fixed rate instead and skip live lookups.
# USD_TO_INR_RATE=96
# FX_RATE_API_URL=https://api.frankfurter.dev/v1/latest?from=USD&to=INR

# ── LiteLLM Proxy (optional — enables hybrid proxy mode) ───────────────
# When LITELLM_PROXY_URL is set, ALL LLM chat calls are routed through
# the LiteLLM proxy. Direct API keys (GEMINI_API_KEY etc.) are still
# required for embeddings (VectorStore RAG). Model names in
# litellm_proxy_config.yaml must match those in framework.config.ts.
# Run proxy: litellm --config litellm_proxy_config.yaml --port 4000
# LITELLM_PROXY_URL=http://localhost:4000
# LITELLM_PROXY_API_KEY=sk-your-litellm-master-key

